@carriers = https://localhost:7049

### 1. FastShip: the first call starts the journey, so the list is empty
GET {{carriers}}/fastship/v2/shipments/FS300001/events

### 2. Send again after ~30 seconds: picked up, in Danish time (+02:00, +01:00 after 25 October)
GET {{carriers}}/fastship/v2/shipments/FS300001/events

### 3. NordPost: the same journey idea in XML, local time without an offset
GET {{carriers}}/nordpost/api/track?barcode=NP300001

### 4. Make FastShip unreliable
PUT {{carriers}}/admin/faults/nordpost
Content-Type: application/json

{ "errorRate": 0.3, "duplicateRate": 0.5, "shuffle": true, "latencyMs": 20000 }

### 5. Send this several times: some 500s, repeated events, random order
GET {{carriers}}/fastship/v2/shipments/FS300001/events

### 6. Now a strict rate limit
PUT {{carriers}}/admin/faults/fastship
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestsPerMinute": 2 }

### 7. Send three times quickly: the third answers 429 with Retry-After: 60
GET {{carriers}}/fastship/v2/shipments/FS300001/events

### 8. Back to normal: faults off, every journey starts again
POST {{carriers}}/admin/reset